WEBVTT

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:08.250
You sure are pumped up today, Wolf.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:10.420
Coach Otaka!

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:12.250
Good morning!

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:16.190
Wolf, why are you so afraid?

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:22.760
If that's true, you won't get any better no matter how much you train.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:25.780
You've been off your game recently.

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:29.220
C-Coach, I can't help it.

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:33.520
I can't get the trapping pit of the Cross Counter out of my head!

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:34.940
Dammit...

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:37.890
That Yabuki won't last much longer.

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:41.680
Yabuki's Cross Counter is old news.

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:50.010
I haven't been part of the Boxing Association for thirty years for nothing!

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:55.100
I've thought up a surefire strategy to defeat him!

00:03:55.850 --> 00:04:00.130
C-Coach, are you telling me you know a way to counter the Cross Counter?

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:03.640
Exactly. And I'm about to teach it to you.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:32.580
How about it, Wolf? Do you see?

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:36.090
Yes. At least, I understand it in theory.

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:42.090
As long as you have the theory down, a technical mind like yours should be able to pull it off.

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.450
R-Right.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.310
Great. Now it's only a matter of time...

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:54.820
...before Yabuki lies at your feet in a pool of his own blood.

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:56.360
Sucks to be him.

00:04:57.140 --> 00:04:59.320
I'll do it, Coach! I'll do it!

00:05:57.800 --> 00:05:59.040
Old man...

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:00.980
What is it?

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:02.820
Has our next match been decided yet?

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:04.050
Yeah.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:07.550
It's on the third of next month.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:10.180
Who are our opponents?

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:12.620
Nishi, you've got Gong Yoshimura,

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:14.690
and Joe, you're up against Noguchi Koichi.

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:17.020
Noguchi? Who's after him?

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:21.690
Takano Yoichi from Oboshi Gym on the 31st.

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:23.770
Takano? And after him?

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:27.740
You're scheduled to take on Suzuki Takekatsu of Yamada Boxing Club.

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:28.990
And after him?

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:31.370
After that, it's...

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:34.560
Hey, old man...

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:38.040
How long are you gonna make me fight small fry, huh?

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:40.300
Who are you calling small fry?

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:44.370
They're all six-rounders, just like you!

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:47.050
But isn't Wolf a six-rounder, too?

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:52.140
Why don't you give me someone like him to fight?

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:56.110
If you keep fighting well and keep up your good record,

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:57.660
I'll let you fight him eventually.

00:06:57.660 --> 00:06:58.900
My good record?

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:01.920
You gotta be kidding. He's not that big a deal.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:13.620
"Yabuki"? You mean, I'm in the paper?

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:14.370
Show me, Nishi!

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:15.540
Don't be so stingy!

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:16.910
Let's see here...

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:21.580
Yabuki's Cross...

00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:23.670
Wh-What the hell!?

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:24.670
Old man!

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:26.340
Have a look at this article!

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:32.310
Yabuki's Cross Counter: "Nothing to Fear."

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:33.440
I see...

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:36.440
No point losing your temper over it.

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:38.690
What's the matter with it, Joe?

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:40.410
What's the matter with it!?

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:42.940
That bastard's so full of himself!

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:45.350
You expect me to let him say whatever the hell he wants?

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:46.400
Well, old man?

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:47.530
Calm down, Joe!

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:50.400
I've already heard Wolf and Coach Otaka's claims.

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:54.170
This is proof that they're panicking about your popularity.

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:59.480
If you just ignore them, they'll send us a formal challenge eventually.

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:03.170
Until then, just continue your matches at your own pace. You hear me?

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:07.230
The hell does he mean by "my own pace"?

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:16.880
It's a letter.

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:20.850
Old man, it's from Coach Otaka from Asia Gym!

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:21.770
Otaka?

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:23.140
Otaka?

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:30.610
Wh-What's it say, old man?

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:32.610
These are...

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:35.110
Tickets to Wolf's match!

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:37.180
Wh-What did you say?

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:39.190
Son of a bitch thinks he's so great...

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:11.440
What a showoff!

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:13.570
This match wasn't even worth watching!

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:16.940
No, Coach Otaka went out of his way to invite us.

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:19.570
There must be something he's trying to tell us.

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:22.330
What would <i>he</i> have to say to us?

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:23.700
I'm going home.

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:25.040
Wait.

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:27.040
Look. Here he comes.

00:09:37.100 --> 00:09:41.100
I'm glad you could make it, Coach Tange, Yabuki Joe-kun.

00:09:42.070 --> 00:09:44.560
Why are all these reporters here?

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:47.160
You'll see soon enough, Yabuki-kun.

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:49.570
Now, gentlemen, are you ready for your scoop?

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:50.800
Scoop?

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:01.290
What's the meaning of this, Otaka-san?

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:06.710
You two are always being tracked by sports reporters these days.

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:10.300
They shouldn't surprise you anymore.

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:14.700
Well, for what it's worth, I thank you for inviting us.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:22.190
And from what we saw of Wolf-kun's match, he's an excellent technical boxer.

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:24.390
I can hardly believe he's still only a six-rounder.

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:27.130
It's only a matter of time till he becomes an eight-rounder.

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:32.700
No, I have no intention of training Wolf to be a boxer...

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:34.780
who only thinks one step ahead.

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:37.560
The world is his oyster! He's aiming at the World Championships!

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:41.260
I see.

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:42.560
That's admirable.

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:48.820
By the way, Coach Tange...

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:52.460
What do you say to a match between Wolf and Yabuki?{TC: does -sen mean challenger?}

00:10:57.890 --> 00:10:59.090
Here it comes.

00:10:59.090 --> 00:10:59.970
Well, Yabuki?

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:03.120
Now that you're winning over the public with your respectable record,

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:05.000
you're ready!

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:06.890
Ready? I've always been...

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:08.040
Joe!

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.940
Don't go saying things you don't have to!

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:12.370
So, Tange...

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:14.360
Here's my suggestion...

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:15.750
Suggestion?

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:16.730
Yes.

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:21.060
Let's just say whoever wins this match gets promoted to the eight-round league.

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:22.260
How's that sound?

00:11:22.730 --> 00:11:24.320
Eight-round league?

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:27.000
Hey, this is getting juicy!

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:29.620
Yeah. The winner becomes an eight-rounder, and the loser stays a six-rounder.

00:11:30.070 --> 00:11:31.790
The fans are gonna love this!

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:33.150
Do it, Yabuki!

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:34.030
Accept, Yabuki!

00:11:34.030 --> 00:11:35.410
You'd better accept the offer!

00:11:36.690 --> 00:11:39.800
Hey, old man! Why aren't you answering?

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:42.260
Old man! Hey!

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:45.300
You're not... You're not gonna refuse, are you?

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:51.240
Old man!

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:52.560
Hey! Old man!

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:53.890
Calm down, Joe!

00:11:53.890 --> 00:11:55.610
Fine, whatever!

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:57.600
If that's the case, I'll respond for him!

00:11:57.600 --> 00:11:58.910
It's on!

00:11:58.910 --> 00:12:00.260
It's definitely on!

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:02.950
I, Yabuki Joe, declare that it's on!

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:04.520
It's on, it's so on!

00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:06.570
Listen up! It's on!

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:04.660
Old man, isn't tonight a great night?

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:13.470
And tonight, the dice of destiny have been cast!

00:13:13.470 --> 00:13:19.340
And the poor, wild Wolf's corpse will be strung up in the ring.

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:22.860
Will you stop talking big already?

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:23.490
What?

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:27.330
If you let it go to your head, it'll come back to bite you in the ass.

00:13:30.340 --> 00:13:32.040
Hey, old man, tell me!

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:35.040
Why do you look so down?

00:13:35.740 --> 00:13:39.580
Shouldn't you be happy that I get to fight a better opponent?

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:41.540
At least congratulate me or something!

00:13:43.570 --> 00:13:44.880
Oh, I get it!

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:50.190
You're upset that I accepted their challenge without your permission!

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:54.070
Old man, you're so easy to read.

00:13:55.670 --> 00:13:57.380
I didn't have a choice!

00:13:58.040 --> 00:14:01.870
They were challenging me. If I hadn't answered, I wouldn't be able to call myself a man!

00:14:02.390 --> 00:14:04.550
Well, Nishi's home alone.

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:06.830
I'll head off to the gym on my own.

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:08.400
Well, see ya!

00:14:55.400 --> 00:14:56.560
Grandfather.

00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:58.620
Wolf and Yabuki-san are finally facing each other.

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:00.970
Yes. Finally.

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:05.780
Yabuki-kun may view everything he's done up till now as a warm-up.

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:07.500
But things will change in his bout with Wolf.

00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:11.930
This is where Yabuki-kun's mettle as a pro boxer will be tested to the fullest.

00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:14.930
I wonder if he's seen this paper yet.

00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:17.010
Yes, I wonder.

00:15:35.770 --> 00:15:38.790
Yabuki Joe, be careful.

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:41.960
Wolf challenged you with an air of confidence about him.

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:44.160
That means he must have figured out how to beat you.

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:47.070
Well, I don't think you'll lose,

00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:51.900
but let's just hope you can still stand in front of me in the ring after being bitten by Wolf's fangs.

00:15:51.900 --> 00:15:53.910
After Wolf, it'll be me, Joe.

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:55.750
Me, Rikiishi Toru.

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:18.500
But man, they're really hyping up Joe's match!

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:21.620
The more this match gets publicized,

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:25.300
the more Joe will be humiliated in print when he loses.

00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:28.000
O-Old man!

00:16:30.430 --> 00:16:36.010
Why are you being so pessimistic about his chances? You're his coach!

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:52.560
What a waste!

00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:56.750
O-Old man, what's the matter?

00:16:58.920 --> 00:17:01.250
I see. You're nervous.

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:03.580
Well, I don't blame ya.

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:06.190
This is the first big match for Tange Gym.

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:08.590
But don't you worry, old man.

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:11.590
Just look at Joe!

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:14.100
He's all fired-up!

00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:14.760
It'll be fine!

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:16.200
He can do this!

00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:33.110
Everyone! Stop your training and listen up!

00:17:44.130 --> 00:17:48.320
Wolf and Yabuki are scheduled to fight three Saturdays from now!

00:17:48.320 --> 00:17:52.130
All of you here should know of Wolf's, or rather Asia Gym's, grudge with Joe.

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:52.900
Yes.

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:53.270
Yes.

00:17:53.270 --> 00:17:54.130
In other words,

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:56.390
it's not just Wolf we're talking about,

00:17:56.390 --> 00:17:58.290
the honor of this gym is on the line!

00:17:58.290 --> 00:18:01.810
This means that Wolf is fighting for the pride of Asia Gym!

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:02.310
And so...

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:06.760
Until Wolf's match is over, all boxers of Asia Gym...

00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:08.270
will support him to the fullest!

00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:08.320
He sure is hustling up there.

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:11.390
His head's filled with thoughts of the fight, now that the match date has been set.

00:19:11.390 --> 00:19:12.710
So, how are you feeling?

00:19:14.240 --> 00:19:15.400
Can't you tell?

00:19:16.220 --> 00:19:18.630
I've never felt better!

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:21.140
What a cool customer! I'm impressed!

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:25.670
I'm more impressed that you all came here,

00:19:25.670 --> 00:19:27.600
instead of following Wolf around, who we all know will lose.

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:29.010
Well, you see, about that...

00:19:29.010 --> 00:19:31.220
Asia Gym's not letting any reporters in.

00:19:31.220 --> 00:19:34.070
Apparently, they're doing some kinda secret training.

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:44.040
"Secret training"?

00:19:44.040 --> 00:19:45.950
O-Old man, what's the matter?

00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:48.890
No, it's nothing.

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:51.670
Sorry, but I don't have any more tea to offer you.

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:02.930
By the way, Yabuki-kun, about Wolf...

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:04.210
W-Wait!

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:08.210
Stop! I beg you, don't interfere with his training any further!

00:20:08.210 --> 00:20:10.020
I'll do the interview in his place!

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:21.910
So, let me put this out there:

00:20:21.910 --> 00:20:24.910
Does Joe have a chance against Wolf Kanagushi?

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:26.250
"A chance"?

00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:31.100
Boxing's a sport where the world champion can get beaten by an unranked fighter.

00:20:31.100 --> 00:20:33.630
We won't know until he tries.

00:20:33.630 --> 00:20:36.420
Oh my, that's not an honest answer at all.

00:20:37.140 --> 00:20:38.420
"Honest"?

00:20:41.490 --> 00:20:43.820
Anyone who talks about chances before a bout...

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:46.510
is either incredibly arrogant or a moron who knows nothing about boxing!

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:52.160
Then, why don't we just say this:

00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:54.020
I may not have a chance, but I'm not gonna lose!

00:20:55.120 --> 00:20:57.140
If I'm knocked down three times, I'll knock him down five!

00:20:57.650 --> 00:21:01.030
And the last man standing will be Yabuki Joe!

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:04.880
Shut up! Be quiet and get on with your training!

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:06.810
F-Fine, I get it!

00:21:06.810 --> 00:21:08.240
Don't get so mad, old man!

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:11.620
He's got a real short fuse.

00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:12.790
Why don't we call it a day?

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:13.930
Well, thank you for your time!

00:21:13.930 --> 00:21:15.040
Sorry to disturb you!

00:21:28.370 --> 00:21:31.260
Old man, why are you so irritable?

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:36.520
My Cross Counter will smash that Wolf bastard to smithereens!

00:21:41.850 --> 00:21:43.560
The Cross Counter...

00:21:48.770 --> 00:21:50.280
Did you say something, old man?{JOE CAN READ THOUGHTS!}

00:21:52.010 --> 00:21:55.250
Joe, do you remember how Wolf's eyes flashed last night?

00:21:55.900 --> 00:21:57.250
Wolf's eyes?

00:21:58.180 --> 00:22:01.170
When Wolf came to see your debut match,

00:22:02.300 --> 00:22:04.570
his eyes shuddered when he saw your Cross Counter.

00:22:05.760 --> 00:22:08.140
They were the fear-filled eyes of a loser.

00:22:08.820 --> 00:22:09.920
But...

00:22:09.920 --> 00:22:12.980
when he appeared before us last night,

00:22:13.750 --> 00:22:16.290
Wolf's eyes were burning like a bright blue flame.

00:22:17.850 --> 00:22:20.560
Can you guess why?

00:22:23.380 --> 00:22:24.480
Come to think of it,

00:22:25.200 --> 00:22:27.510
he did look strangely calm!

00:22:28.840 --> 00:22:30.950
And today, he's doing some secret training.

00:22:33.150 --> 00:22:34.210
Listen, Joe.

00:22:34.630 --> 00:22:36.050
Do not underestimate Wolf.

00:22:36.050 --> 00:22:37.750
He's no longer a wild dog...

00:22:37.750 --> 00:22:40.210
He may be a fully-fledged wolf with mighty fangs for all we know!

00:22:40.920 --> 00:22:42.540
Hey! I've got some news!

00:22:43.210 --> 00:22:47.620
This report from Ishida, the boxing commentator, just landed on my desk!

00:22:47.620 --> 00:22:48.510
According to him,

00:22:48.510 --> 00:22:53.050
Wolf's secret training likely revolves around a new strategy to counter Yabuki's Cross Counter!

00:22:53.050 --> 00:22:55.030
What? Counter the Cross Counter?

00:22:55.030 --> 00:22:55.520
Yeah!

00:22:55.520 --> 00:22:57.420
How's that even possible?

00:22:57.420 --> 00:23:02.540
You dunce. If we knew that, it'd hardly be secret training!

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:06.490
C-Counter the Cross Counter?

00:23:21.250 --> 00:23:22.660
The Cross Counter...

00:23:23.690 --> 00:23:24.960
I knew it.

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:26.580
That's the problem.

00:23:26.580 --> 00:23:28.230
The Cross Counter...

00:23:28.230 --> 00:23:29.730
That's the problem!

00:23:41.500 --> 00:23:43.520
The showdown between Wolf and Joe is drawing near.

00:23:44.710 --> 00:23:48.530
The children sneak into Asia Gym to discover the meaning behind Wolf's secret training,

00:23:49.530 --> 00:23:52.180
but Wolf sends them packing, covered in scars.

00:23:52.830 --> 00:23:55.540
Joe sheds tears at the sorry sight of them.

00:23:56.580 --> 00:24:01.600
Now, for Joe, sweating through his own furious training,

00:24:01.600 --> 00:24:03.070
which way is tomorrow!?
